# kex: skip-beam
# A template with no holes at all lowers to a genuinely zero-parameter
# function (kexhq/kex#171 M3) — free-variable inference finds nothing, so
# `params` stays empty and the call takes no arguments.
#
# skip-beam: a zero-arg function reached through `~name` auto-calls on
# BEAM instead of yielding the function value (kexhq/kex#312, found while
# writing this spec) — general breakage, unrelated to templates, that
# happens to be exactly what a holeless template's generated reference is
# shaped like. Works correctly on the tree-walker.

main do
  let banner = Template.text(`Kex.
No holes here.`)
  IO.printLine(banner())
end
